WEBVTT

1
00:04:05.661 --> 00:04:08.789
My mommy always said
there were no monsters.

2
00:04:08.897 --> 00:04:10.956
No real ones.

3
00:04:13.068 --> 00:04:15.332
But there are.

4
00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:24.306
She's perfect.

5
00:04:51.974 --> 00:04:54.442
Careful.

6
00:04:54.509 --> 00:04:56.977
Two centimeters.

7
00:05:02.184 --> 00:05:05.676
Yeah. Ready with that amnio.

8
00:05:11.293 --> 00:05:12.817
And...

9
00:05:17.733 --> 00:05:19.462
there it is.

10
00:05:33.982 --> 00:05:37.042
But be careful.

11
00:05:43.825 --> 00:05:45.725
Jesus!

12
00:05:48.664 --> 00:05:50.894
Clamp.

13
00:05:51.533 --> 00:05:54.696
What about her? Can we keep her alive?

14
00:05:55.737 --> 00:05:57.568
How's the host?

15
00:05:59.441 --> 00:06:01.739
Doing well.

16
00:06:04.513 --> 00:06:06.913
Sew her back up.

17
00:06:10.419 --> 00:06:12.717
Excellent work. Everybody.

18
00:07:55.174 --> 00:08:00.544
- How is our Number Eight today?
- Appears to be in good health.

19
00:08:00.613 --> 00:08:02.581
- How good?
- Excellent.

20
00:08:02.682 --> 00:08:06.083
As in completely off our projected charts.

21
00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:09.681
Look at the scar tissue.

22
00:08:12.792 --> 00:08:14.760
See the recession?

23
00:08:14.861 --> 00:08:17.853
- This is from three days ago?
- Exactly.

24
00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:20.057
Well. this is good.

25
00:08:20.132 --> 00:08:22.225
This is very good.

26
00:08:24.136 --> 00:08:27.264
You're gonna make us all very proud.

27
00:08:44.891 --> 00:08:47.519
Don't! I'm all right!

28
00:08:57.803 --> 00:09:00.499
- Hand.
- Close.

29
00:09:00.606 --> 00:09:02.665
Glove.

30
00:09:12.451 --> 00:09:14.942
Number Eight?

31
00:09:15.021 --> 00:09:18.081
- Fruit.
- Good. Cherries.

32
00:09:18.157 --> 00:09:21.092
- It's unprecedented.
- Totally.

33
00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:26.154
She's operating at
a completely adult capacity.

34
00:09:27.934 --> 00:09:30.801
- What about her memories?
- There are gaps.

35
00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:34.169
Some degree of synaptic dissonance.

36
00:09:34.273 --> 00:09:36.104
She's freaked.

37
00:09:36.175 --> 00:09:41.772
It has difficulties. caused by a biochemical
imbalance. causing emotional autism...

38
00:09:41.847 --> 00:09:44.680
Wait a second. It has memories!

39
00:09:44.784 --> 00:09:46.877
Why does it have memories?

40
00:09:46.986 --> 00:09:49.784
I'm guessing. but inherited memories.

41
00:09:49.855 --> 00:09:54.019
passed down generationally by the aliens.
like its strength.

42
00:09:55.061 --> 00:09:58.553
Plus a highly evolved form of instinct.

43
00:10:06.485 --> 00:10:07.884
Of course.

44
00:10:07.987 --> 00:10:13.391
An unexpected benefit of the genetic process!
I didn't even think of that!

45
00:10:14.860 --> 00:10:17.328
Let's try this one.

46
00:10:21.033 --> 00:10:23.126
Ripley?

47
00:10:24.570 --> 00:10:26.663
Ripley?

48
00:10:28.207 --> 00:10:30.505
Ripley. what is it?

49
00:10:32.578 --> 00:10:34.671
Ripley? Ripley?

50
00:10:40.252 --> 00:10:43.710
- You're not thinking termination?
- Oh. boy. am I!

51
00:10:43.823 --> 00:10:46.018
General. this is not a problem.

52
00:10:46.092 --> 00:10:48.822
Ellen Ripley died
trying to wipe this species out.

53
00:10:48.894 --> 00:10:51.362
For all intents and purposes. she succeeded.

54
00:10:51.430 --> 00:10:53.694
I don't want her taking up old hobbies.

55
00:10:53.766 --> 00:10:56.326
- That won't happen.
- We won't tell her.

56
00:10:56.502 --> 00:11:00.268
Oh. I see. And that's supposed to comfort me.

57
00:11:01.740 --> 00:11:05.767
Identification. please.

58
00:11:07.546 --> 00:11:09.673
Please try again.

59
00:11:09.748 --> 00:11:12.080
Thank you. General Perez.

60
00:11:12.184 --> 00:11:17.349
The bottom line is. she looks at me funny
one time. I'm putting her down.

61
00:11:17.423 --> 00:11:23.089
OK. as far as I'm concerned
Number Eight is a meat by-product.

62
00:11:26.699 --> 00:11:29.930
Her Majesty here is the real payoff.

63
00:11:30.035 --> 00:11:32.595
- When does she start producing?
- Days.

64
00:11:32.705 --> 00:11:34.570
Less. maybe.

65
00:11:34.640 --> 00:11:38.371
- We need the cargo.
- I told you. it's on its way.

66
00:12:16.649 --> 00:12:18.640
Fork.

67
00:12:19.685 --> 00:12:23.018
- Fuck.
- It's a fork.

68
00:12:26.959 --> 00:12:29.291
How did you...

69
00:12:30.496 --> 00:12:33.021
How did we get you?

70
00:12:34.033 --> 00:12:35.625
Yes.

71
00:12:39.338 --> 00:12:44.776
Hard work. We used blood samples.
from Fiori 16. on ice.

72
00:12:44.843 --> 00:12:46.936
Where you died.

73
00:12:47.012 --> 00:12:50.038
We've remade you. We cloned you.

74
00:12:51.116 --> 00:12:53.380
Fiori 16.

75
00:12:55.487 --> 00:12:58.047
Does that ring a bell?

76
00:12:58.157 --> 00:13:00.955
Are you remembering something?

77
00:13:02.228 --> 00:13:04.492
Does it grow?

78
00:13:04.563 --> 00:13:07.464
Yeah. Very rapidly.

79
00:13:09.902 --> 00:13:13.998
- It's a queen.
- How did you know that?

80
00:13:15.341 --> 00:13:17.673
She'll breed.

81
00:13:17.743 --> 00:13:19.802
You'll die.

82
00:13:19.878 --> 00:13:22.472
Everyone in the company will die.

83
00:13:22.548 --> 00:13:24.345
In the company?

84
00:13:24.416 --> 00:13:28.910
Weyland-Yutani.
Ripley Eight's former employers.

85
00:13:29.021 --> 00:13:34.516
A terran growth conglomerate. They had
defense contracts under the military.

86
00:13:34.593 --> 00:13:38.495
They went under decades ago. Gediman.
Way before your time.

87
00:13:38.564 --> 00:13:41.158
Bought out by Wal-Mart.

88
00:13:42.067 --> 00:13:44.433
Fortunes of war.

89
00:13:45.504 --> 00:13:51.272
I think you will find that things have
changed a great deal since your time.

90
00:13:51.377 --> 00:13:53.845
I doubt that.

91
00:13:53.912 --> 00:13:59.851
We're not flying blind. This is United Systems
Military. not some greedy corporation.

92
00:14:01.587 --> 00:14:04.556
Well. it won't make any difference.

93
00:14:05.724 --> 00:14:08.022
You're still gonna die.

94
00:14:09.928 --> 00:14:12.260
How do you feel about that?

95
00:14:17.102 --> 00:14:19.570
I wish you understood
what we're trying to do.

96
00:14:19.638 --> 00:14:25.543
The potential for this species goes beyond
urban pacification: new alloys. new vaccines.

97
00:14:25.611 --> 00:14:28.546
Nothing like this
we've ever seen on any world.

98
00:14:28.614 --> 00:14:30.946
You should be very proud.

99
00:14:33.052 --> 00:14:34.781
I am.

100
00:14:34.887 --> 00:14:37.481
And the animal itself.

101
00:14:37.589 --> 00:14:39.716
wondrous.

102
00:14:39.792 --> 00:14:44.126
The potential. unbelievable.
Once we've tamed him.

103
00:14:45.931 --> 00:14:48.764
Roll over? Play dead?

104
00:14:48.834 --> 00:14:50.631
Heel?

105
00:14:51.236 --> 00:14:53.295
You can't teach it tricks.

106
00:14:53.839 --> 00:14:57.331
Why not? We're teaching you.

107
00:15:13.492 --> 00:15:16.791
Hey. son. I'll give you
my authorization code.

108
00:15:16.862 --> 00:15:20.263
It's E-A-T-M-E.

109
00:15:20.332 --> 00:15:22.823
Could you repeat that?

110
00:15:22.935 --> 00:15:25.165
Little prick.

111
00:15:25.270 --> 00:15:28.933
You know. no matter
how many times you see it.

112
00:15:29.007 --> 00:15:34.309
the sight of a woman all strapped up
in a chair like thatjust...

113
00:15:36.482 --> 00:15:38.040
What?

114
00:15:38.150 --> 00:15:41.642
Just bring us in on a 3-0 descent.
And ride the parallel.

115
00:15:41.720 --> 00:15:44.484
- Darling. it is done.
- Good girl.

116
00:15:45.491 --> 00:15:48.688
You want anything?

117
00:15:48.794 --> 00:15:52.059
Yeah. How about a cup of coffee?

118
00:15:52.164 --> 00:15:55.327
Anything else while your mouth's warm?

119
00:15:55.401 --> 00:15:57.562
A little milk.

120
00:16:00.005 --> 00:16:04.567
Hey. don't cut thrust till about 600 meters.
We'll give 'em a little scare.

121
00:16:05.210 --> 00:16:06.677
Vriess! Call!

122
00:16:06.745 --> 00:16:09.043
Goddamn. we're gonna die!

123
00:16:33.272 --> 00:16:35.365
- Hey. Call?
- Yeah?

124
00:16:36.909 --> 00:16:40.345
What has two thumbs. one eye.

125
00:16:41.580 --> 00:16:43.673
a pink tongue.

126
00:16:44.750 --> 00:16:47.548
and screws like a god?

127
00:16:49.221 --> 00:16:50.848
What?

128
00:16:57.896 --> 00:17:01.730
Two thumbs. one eye. a pink tongue.

129
00:17:01.800 --> 00:17:04.633
and screws like a god?

130
00:17:07.372 --> 00:17:08.464
What?

131
00:17:23.722 --> 00:17:28.421
Time to enjoy some of
the general's hospitality. Christie.

132
00:17:28.494 --> 00:17:30.621
Great. Army food.

133
00:17:30.729 --> 00:17:34.722
Yeah. it'll do till we get
the family wagon up to spec.

134
00:17:36.235 --> 00:17:39.398
That is. if the natives are friendly.

135
00:17:39.471 --> 00:17:42.099
- How's that?
- Good.

136
00:17:42.975 --> 00:17:45.808
Are we expecting any trouble?

137
00:17:45.911 --> 00:17:49.938
From Perez. I doubt it. But you never know -
we've been there before.

138
00:18:04.930 --> 00:18:07.660
What is wrong with you?

139
00:18:07.766 --> 00:18:10.326
Just a little target practice.

140
00:18:11.770 --> 00:18:14.466
Vriess isn't complaining.

141
00:18:15.707 --> 00:18:17.937
Goddammit!

142
00:18:18.010 --> 00:18:22.344
- Johner. you son of a bitch!
- Come on. man. you didn't feel a thing.

143
00:18:27.719 --> 00:18:30.711
You are an inbred motherfucker.
you know that?

144
00:18:36.328 --> 00:18:38.694
I'll take the knife back now.

145
00:18:43.168 --> 00:18:44.658
Whoa...

146
00:18:45.404 --> 00:18:48.168
Call. forget it.

147
00:18:48.807 --> 00:18:51.537
He's been sucking down
too much home-brew.

148
00:18:53.912 --> 00:18:56.005
The knife.

149
00:18:58.717 --> 00:19:00.582
Son of a bitch!

150
00:19:02.654 --> 00:19:05.384
Don't push me.
You hang with us for a while.

151
00:19:05.490 --> 00:19:09.654
you'll find out I am not the man
with whom to fuck.

152
00:19:18.770 --> 00:19:24.606
It's about time we started associating
with a better class of people.

153
00:20:09.809 --> 00:20:11.936
I am Father.

154
00:20:12.011 --> 00:20:14.912
Welcome to the USM Auriga.

155
00:20:14.981 --> 00:20:18.644
Step forward for contraband
and weapons search.

156
00:20:18.751 --> 00:20:23.518
Please report any infectious diseases
to the medical officers.

157
00:20:23.623 --> 00:20:27.855
Levels seven through twelve
are off-limits to civilians.

158
00:20:27.961 --> 00:20:30.794
Thank you for your cooperation.

159
00:20:30.863 --> 00:20:32.660
Go.

160
00:20:35.368 --> 00:20:37.996
- Hands up. please.
- What?

161
00:20:38.938 --> 00:20:41.429
Could you get your hands up. please?

162
00:20:50.149 --> 00:20:53.141
No weapons allowed on board. sir.

163
00:20:54.320 --> 00:20:56.720
My own recipe.

164
00:20:57.857 --> 00:20:59.984
Way more dangerous.

165
00:21:03.630 --> 00:21:07.122
Nice welcome. Perez. What the hell is this?

166
00:21:07.200 --> 00:21:10.727
Are you afraid the six of us
are gonna hijack your damn ship?

167
00:21:10.837 --> 00:21:14.170
Just the concern that
one of your asshole crew members

168
00:21:14.240 --> 00:21:19.143
is gonna get drunk and put a bullet through
the hull. We happen to be in space.

169
00:21:19.212 --> 00:21:20.839
No shit.

170
00:21:20.913 --> 00:21:23.006
How you been?

171
00:21:30.690 --> 00:21:32.988
Wanna check the chair?

172
00:21:38.131 --> 00:21:41.532
Elgyn. these were very. very hard to come by.

173
00:21:41.601 --> 00:21:43.660
So was our cargo.

174
00:21:44.103 --> 00:21:47.595
You're not about to plead poverty on me.
are you. General?

175
00:21:47.707 --> 00:21:50.938
No. I'm just saying.
very few people deal in cash nowadays.

176
00:21:51.044 --> 00:21:55.777
Just the ones don't like to keep
business records. Yourself. for example.

177
00:21:55.882 --> 00:21:58.612
- Drink. Elgyn?
- Constantly.

178
00:22:03.222 --> 00:22:07.386
I'm gonna take a wild guess here. General.
but I'm thinking

179
00:22:08.127 --> 00:22:13.963
whatever you got going on here.
it ain't exactly approved by Congress.

180
00:22:15.034 --> 00:22:20.199
Who's the new filly
you got on board. Elgyn?

181
00:22:20.273 --> 00:22:21.740
Call?

182
00:22:24.526 --> 00:22:26.016
She makes an impression.

183
00:22:28.009 --> 00:22:30.876
She is severely fuckable. ain't she?

184
00:22:37.752 --> 00:22:41.313
Mighty handy with a monkey wrench. too.
I might add.

185
00:22:41.389 --> 00:22:44.916
I think Vriess has got
a bit of a light in his eye for her.

186
00:22:45.026 --> 00:22:49.759
Fine little ass like that make a man walk.
you know what I mean?

187
00:22:53.334 --> 00:22:58.863
Mind you. I think she's just a tad curious
about this transaction of ours.

188
00:22:59.006 --> 00:23:03.875
I can't say as I blame her.
It's awfully cloak-and-dagger stuff.

189
00:23:04.945 --> 00:23:07.675
It's a military operation.

190
00:23:07.748 --> 00:23:09.511
Really?

191
00:23:09.583 --> 00:23:14.850
Correct me if I'm wrong.
but I was under the impression that

192
00:23:14.922 --> 00:23:19.416
most army medical labs don't operate
outside of regulated space.

193
00:23:19.527 --> 00:23:22.052
What do you want?
What can I do for you?

194
00:23:22.129 --> 00:23:24.063
- Me?
- Yeah.

195
00:23:24.131 --> 00:23:26.224
Two days' bed and board.

196
00:23:26.300 --> 00:23:31.431
Vriess might want to snag a part or two.
I mean. if it's not imposing.

197
00:23:31.539 --> 00:23:34.406
I don't see any problem.

198
00:23:34.475 --> 00:23:37.933
- A couple of conditions. though.
- Ah. conditions.

199
00:23:40.114 --> 00:23:46.781
Not you. nor any of your
formidable crew members.

200
00:23:47.321 --> 00:23:51.121
will go anywhere near restricted areas.

201
00:23:51.759 --> 00:23:53.818
Rule number two.

202
00:23:55.563 --> 00:23:59.465
- No trouble. Good behavior.
- Good behavior.

203
00:23:59.967 --> 00:24:02.299
- No fights.
- No fights?

204
00:24:02.403 --> 00:24:05.998
- No fights.
- No fights.

205
00:24:07.508 --> 00:24:09.908
Mi casa es su casa.

206
00:24:34.306 --> 00:24:38.640
Please direct cargo to medlab centre. area G.

207
00:24:39.778 --> 00:24:42.178
Follow the lit path.

208
00:24:42.280 --> 00:24:44.646
Do not deviate.

209
00:24:55.627 --> 00:24:58.118
Cargo status stable.

210
00:24:58.196 --> 00:25:00.926
Life forms intact.

211
00:25:00.999 --> 00:25:03.661
Stasis uninterrupted.

212
00:25:16.047 --> 00:25:20.484
Medlab centre is off-limits to civilians.

213
00:25:20.552 --> 00:25:22.645
Thank you.

214
00:26:35.794 --> 00:26:39.252
- Oh. please.
- You know I can't lay off the tall ones.

215
00:26:39.364 --> 00:26:41.059
How ya doin'?

216
00:26:41.132 --> 00:26:44.624
How about a little one-on-one?
Whaddaya say?

217
00:26:50.542 --> 00:26:53.409
You got some moves on you. girl.

218
00:27:16.601 --> 00:27:21.732
If you don't wanna play basketball.
I know some other indoor sports.

219
00:27:33.018 --> 00:27:35.486
Come on. now. give me the ball.

220
00:27:46.498 --> 00:27:49.524
OK... I got a new game.

221
00:27:49.968 --> 00:27:50.935
Tag.

222
00:28:06.051 --> 00:28:07.279
Ripley!

223
00:28:07.552 --> 00:28:08.780
Ripley.

224
00:28:15.660 --> 00:28:18.060
You've had enough fun.

225
00:28:21.032 --> 00:28:23.159
What the hell are you?

226
00:28:33.378 --> 00:28:35.471
Something of a predator. isn't she?

227
00:28:35.547 --> 00:28:39.643
Yes. she continues to make us all very proud.

228
00:29:54.926 --> 00:30:00.626
There's just one minute and 30 seconds left
to order this collector's item.

229
00:30:00.732 --> 00:30:05.465
Jesus Christ. Johner.
what did you put in this shit? Battery acid?

230
00:30:05.570 --> 00:30:06.901
Just for colour.

231
00:32:14.866 --> 00:32:17.767
So. we're a fast learner.

232
00:32:19.771 --> 00:32:23.298
This is a really good show. man.

233
00:32:40.658 --> 00:32:44.253
Woman. that shit is not easy to come by!

234
00:32:44.329 --> 00:32:47.457
Why don't you take a walk outside?

235
00:32:52.804 --> 00:32:53.429
Great!

236
00:32:53.504 --> 00:32:56.166
I'm so sorry.

237
00:32:56.274 --> 00:33:02.577
If bitches can't handle this shit.
they should stay away from this shit!

238
00:33:26.371 --> 00:33:29.135
Identification. please.

239
00:33:34.112 --> 00:33:36.171
Please try again.

240
00:33:39.884 --> 00:33:42.512
Please try again.

241
00:33:45.223 --> 00:33:47.817
Thank you. General Perez.

242
00:34:23.194 --> 00:34:24.525
Well?

243
00:34:27.365 --> 00:34:30.266
Are you gonna kill me. or what?

244
00:34:31.769 --> 00:34:33.862
There's no point. is there?

245
00:34:33.938 --> 00:34:36.236
They've taken it out of you.

246
00:34:36.340 --> 00:34:39.537
Where is it? Is it on the ship?

247
00:34:41.245 --> 00:34:43.543
You mean my "baby"?

248
00:34:45.249 --> 00:34:50.380
I don't get it. If they took it out.
why are they keeping you alive?

249
00:34:50.455 --> 00:34:54.687
Well. they're curious. I'm the latest thing.

250
00:35:03.768 --> 00:35:07.397
Look. I can make it all stop.

251
00:35:08.039 --> 00:35:11.475
The pain. this nightmare.
That's all I can offer you.

252
00:35:19.951 --> 00:35:23.717
What makes you think
I would let you do that?

253
00:35:28.392 --> 00:35:30.257
Who are you?

254
00:35:30.328 --> 00:35:33.889
Ripley. Ellen. Lieutenant First Class.

255
00:35:33.965 --> 00:35:36.058
Number 36706.

256
00:35:38.936 --> 00:35:41.666
Ellen Ripley died 200 years ago.

257
00:35:43.007 --> 00:35:45.305
You're not her.

258
00:35:46.410 --> 00:35:48.810
I'm not her?

259
00:35:55.353 --> 00:35:59.414
- Who am I?
- You're a thing. a construct.

260
00:35:59.490 --> 00:36:02.516
They grew you in a fucking lab.

261
00:36:03.027 --> 00:36:05.689
And now they brought it out of you.

262
00:36:05.796 --> 00:36:07.991
Not all the way out.

263
00:36:13.971 --> 00:36:16.496
I can feel it.

264
00:36:16.607 --> 00:36:19.371
Behind my eyes.

265
00:36:19.477 --> 00:36:21.536
I can hear it moving.

266
00:36:25.983 --> 00:36:28.508
Help me stop this thing before it gets loose.

267
00:36:32.723 --> 00:36:34.850
It's too late.

268
00:36:34.959 --> 00:36:37.621
You can't stop it.

269
00:36:37.695 --> 00:36:39.788
It's inevitable.

270
00:36:42.867 --> 00:36:45.631
Not as long as I'm around.

271
00:36:45.703 --> 00:36:48.137
You'll never get out of here alive.

272
00:36:49.140 --> 00:36:51.904
I don't care.

273
00:36:52.009 --> 00:36:53.840
Really?

274
00:36:56.347 --> 00:36:58.406
I can make it stop.

275
00:37:05.356 --> 00:37:08.325
Go on. get out of here.

276
00:37:08.392 --> 00:37:10.553
They're looking for you.

277
00:37:22.273 --> 00:37:27.336
I think you're gonna find that this was
very ill-advised. Where are her friends?

278
00:37:27.411 --> 00:37:32.007
- They're in the mess hall. sir.
- Well. you find them. now. Quietly!

279
00:37:32.383 --> 00:37:37.878
- What the hell is goin' on here?
- Smells like a double-cross. boss.

280
00:37:37.955 --> 00:37:41.254
Where's the other one? With the chair?

281
00:37:41.359 --> 00:37:44.590
Don't ever touch me. Ever!

282
00:37:45.429 --> 00:37:49.058
- Wanna tell us what this is?
- Wanna tell me who you're working for?

283
00:37:49.133 --> 00:37:52.466
- Wren. they got nothing to do with this.
- To do with what?

284
00:37:52.570 --> 00:37:55.471
Do you know the penalties
for terrorist activity?

285
00:37:55.573 --> 00:37:58.599
No terrorists in my crew.
Call. got something to say?

286
00:37:58.709 --> 00:38:03.305
I don't care whether you knew or not.
You brought a terrorist on board.

287
00:38:03.447 --> 00:38:06.780
And as far as I am concerned.
you all die with her!

288
00:38:08.886 --> 00:38:10.945
Do you understand?

289
00:38:13.057 --> 00:38:15.287
Yeah.

290
00:38:15.393 --> 00:38:17.452
I understand.

291
00:38:20.064 --> 00:38:21.156
Christie.

292
00:38:29.640 --> 00:38:30.971
Freeze!

293
00:38:39.250 --> 00:38:41.514
Stop! Drop your weapons!

294
00:38:41.652 --> 00:38:45.486
And you. drop that piece of shit!
Or I blow his head off!

295
00:38:45.556 --> 00:38:47.990
- I can't do that. man.
- Drop it now!

296
00:38:48.059 --> 00:38:50.550
- They're attached.
- I'm not fucking with you!

297
00:38:50.661 --> 00:38:53.892
You're all under arrest
for a Code 8. concealed weapons.

298
00:38:53.998 --> 00:38:56.228
and a Code 12. which is murder!

299
00:38:56.334 --> 00:38:59.167
- Kiss my ass.
- Put down your weapons!

300
00:39:05.509 --> 00:39:08.000
Everybody OK?

301
00:39:10.314 --> 00:39:13.181
Real easy. soldier boy.

302
00:39:13.250 --> 00:39:18.153
Security! There is a serious problem
in the mess hall.

303
00:39:18.222 --> 00:39:21.020
You lie to me now. little girl.

304
00:39:22.760 --> 00:39:24.921
I will cut your throat.

305
00:39:27.698 --> 00:39:29.427
- We do not read you.
- Hello?

306
00:39:29.533 --> 00:39:32.661
- We do not copy you. Please repeat.
- Hello?

307
00:41:07.798 --> 00:41:09.766
Gediman.

308
00:41:09.834 --> 00:41:12.667
He's conducting illegal experiments.
breeding...

309
00:41:12.770 --> 00:41:17.707
- Ice the goddamn mole!
- Listen! He is breeding an alien species.

310
00:41:17.808 --> 00:41:20.777
If it gets loose.
it'll make the Lacerta plague

311
00:41:20.845 --> 00:41:23.712
- Look like a fucking square dance.
- Shut up!

312
00:41:26.784 --> 00:41:27.978
Listen.

313
00:41:29.653 --> 00:41:32.645
Your attention. please. Security breach.

314
00:41:32.857 --> 00:41:34.950
Medlab. level 15.

315
00:42:29.847 --> 00:42:33.442
Let's get back to the Betty.
The doctor and soldier boy can escort us.

316
00:42:33.517 --> 00:42:34.814
What about Vriess?

317
00:42:46.764 --> 00:42:48.857
Your attention. please.

318
00:42:48.933 --> 00:42:52.266
Unauthorised opening of cage three.

319
00:42:52.369 --> 00:42:55.896
Unauthorised opening of cages five.

320
00:42:55.973 --> 00:42:59.431
seven. eight. ten.

321
00:42:59.543 --> 00:43:01.807
- Move it!
- Evacuation.

322
00:43:01.912 --> 00:43:04.938
- Go! Go! Go!
- Evacuation.

323
00:43:15.292 --> 00:43:17.624
This is not a drill.

324
00:43:26.804 --> 00:43:29.329
- Evacuation.
- Get on board!

325
00:43:30.441 --> 00:43:34.002
Your attention. please.
Non-human presence detected.

326
00:43:34.678 --> 00:43:37.841
Levels 21. 23.

327
00:43:38.582 --> 00:43:40.277
27.

328
00:43:40.351 --> 00:43:41.818
14.

329
00:43:41.919 --> 00:43:44.149
Level 38.

330
00:43:44.254 --> 00:43:46.415
Level 39.

331
00:43:48.125 --> 00:43:51.094
Evacuation. Proceed to lifeboats.

332
00:43:52.630 --> 00:43:54.621
This is not a drill.

333
00:43:54.698 --> 00:43:57.531
Thank you for your cooperation.

334
00:45:04.101 --> 00:45:07.264
I'll give you holes. you slimy bastard!

335
00:45:12.076 --> 00:45:13.338
Move it! Go!

336
00:45:13.410 --> 00:45:16.072
- Final lifeboat ready for launch.
- Get aboard!

337
00:45:22.453 --> 00:45:23.511
Go!

338
00:45:23.587 --> 00:45:26.420
Complete evacuation now.

339
00:45:35.232 --> 00:45:36.790
Grenade.

340
00:46:33.023 --> 00:46:35.287
Evacuation incomplete.

341
00:46:36.260 --> 00:46:39.957
Civilian presence detected in area H.

342
00:46:40.030 --> 00:46:43.966
Warning: main vessel declared uninhabitable.

343
00:46:52.209 --> 00:46:56.771
- Elgyn. come on. Let's move. man.
- Yeah.

344
00:48:16.093 --> 00:48:19.426
Elgyn! Elgyn. where are you?

345
00:48:33.944 --> 00:48:36.037
Elgyn!

346
00:49:13.517 --> 00:49:15.610
Elgyn!

347
00:49:16.253 --> 00:49:17.584
Elgyn!

348
00:49:24.194 --> 00:49:25.821
Easy. Hillard!

349
00:49:25.929 --> 00:49:28.523
- Give me a hand here!
- Get him up!

350
00:49:29.333 --> 00:49:32.131
- Come on. let's get him up!
- Move out of the way!

351
00:49:32.202 --> 00:49:33.794
Aw. shit.

352
00:49:33.870 --> 00:49:36.805
- What the fuck did this?
- What's in this place?

353
00:49:43.447 --> 00:49:45.881
- Call. get down!
- What the fuck is that?

354
00:49:45.983 --> 00:49:48.884
Don't shoot!
It's in front of the hull!

355
00:49:51.054 --> 00:49:54.490
- What is that?
- Come on. man. time to go.

356
00:49:54.558 --> 00:49:55.616
Get back!

357
00:49:58.662 --> 00:50:00.323
Time to go!

358
00:50:00.397 --> 00:50:01.887
Come on. Call!

359
00:50:01.999 --> 00:50:04.126
Open the goddamn door!

360
00:50:04.201 --> 00:50:09.229
We can't open it! We can't open the door!

361
00:50:13.377 --> 00:50:17.746
- We gotta go back!
- I'm not going back. You go back.

362
00:50:43.073 --> 00:50:44.870
What the fuck...?

363
00:50:47.377 --> 00:50:50.107
Was it everything you hoped for?

364
00:50:51.248 --> 00:50:53.341
Leave him alone.

365
00:51:02.426 --> 00:51:05.190
What do we do now. man?

366
00:51:05.262 --> 00:51:08.527
Same thing we were doing.
We get the hell outta here.

367
00:51:08.598 --> 00:51:10.896
What if there's more?

368
00:51:10.967 --> 00:51:14.903
I say we stay here. man.
Let the army guys deal.

369
00:51:14.971 --> 00:51:19.374
- Where the fuck are the army guys?
- They're dead.

370
00:51:19.443 --> 00:51:22.378
- Then we don't need this asshole.
- Step back!

371
00:51:22.446 --> 00:51:24.141
- You!
- Stop!

372
00:51:24.247 --> 00:51:26.977
You got no authority here!

373
00:51:28.752 --> 00:51:31.619
Doctor. that thing that killed my partner.

374
00:51:31.721 --> 00:51:35.213
- That's your pet science project?
- Yes.

375
00:51:35.325 --> 00:51:38.692
- Let me do him!
- I should let him do you right now.

376
00:51:39.129 --> 00:51:41.063
How many more are there?

377
00:51:41.298 --> 00:51:43.596
How many more are there?

378
00:51:43.667 --> 00:51:45.760
Twelve.

379
00:51:47.471 --> 00:51:49.530
Twelve?

380
00:51:49.639 --> 00:51:51.129
Twelve.

381
00:51:53.376 --> 00:51:55.708
Twelve.

382
00:51:55.812 --> 00:51:57.871
There'll be more.

383
00:51:59.349 --> 00:52:04.616
So. who do I have to fuck
to get off this boat?

384
00:52:07.324 --> 00:52:10.782
I can get you off. Maybe not the boat. but...

385
00:52:12.562 --> 00:52:13.824
Let's go.

386
00:52:13.897 --> 00:52:17.230
No. wait a second.
She was the host for these monsters.

387
00:52:17.334 --> 00:52:20.565
Wren cloned her
because she had one inside her.

388
00:52:20.670 --> 00:52:22.399
She's not human.

389
00:52:23.140 --> 00:52:26.507
She was part of his experiment.
She will turn on us in a second.

390
00:52:26.576 --> 00:52:30.068
- I don't give a shit what she is.
- She's too much of a risk.

391
00:52:30.180 --> 00:52:32.478
- We have to leave her.
- She comes.

392
00:52:32.983 --> 00:52:36.384
- We can't trust her.
- I don't trust anyone.

393
00:52:40.590 --> 00:52:46.187
If we're gonna survive this mess.
we all stick together. Agreed?

394
00:52:56.606 --> 00:52:58.335
Hillard. we gotta go.

395
00:52:58.408 --> 00:53:00.774
It's not over. We gotta get to the Betty.

396
00:53:29.773 --> 00:53:31.866
Make a nice souvenir.

397
00:53:40.398 --> 00:53:44.198
- I can't believe you did that.
- Did what?

398
00:53:44.302 --> 00:53:46.566
Killed one.
It's like killing your own kind.

399
00:53:46.671 --> 00:53:48.730
It was in my way.

400
00:54:12.063 --> 00:54:14.088
Oh. man!

401
00:54:18.402 --> 00:54:21.394
Who were you expecting? Santa Claus?

402
00:54:22.373 --> 00:54:25.365
I thought you were toast for certain. man.

403
00:54:25.843 --> 00:54:28.209
Where's Elgyn?

404
00:54:31.682 --> 00:54:34.776
- Shit.
- What if they're all over the Betty?

405
00:54:34.885 --> 00:54:38.013
All the activity was in the F sector.
Why would they move?

406
00:54:38.089 --> 00:54:43.254
They won't. If they send anyone out.
it'll be here.

407
00:54:44.395 --> 00:54:46.556
Where the meat is.

408
00:54:46.631 --> 00:54:50.863
Yeah... If we wanna make any decent time.
I say we ditch the cripple.

409
00:54:52.770 --> 00:54:55.637
- No offence. man.
- None taken.

410
00:54:55.740 --> 00:54:57.765
Nobody is left behind.

411
00:54:57.875 --> 00:55:00.537
Not even you. Johner.

412
00:55:01.779 --> 00:55:06.216
- What's the quickest way out?
- After the cooling tower. there's an elevator.

413
00:55:06.283 --> 00:55:09.719
It runs from the top of the ship
down to level one.

414
00:55:09.787 --> 00:55:13.985
- Straight to the dock.
- Sounds reasonable. Let's do it.

415
00:55:15.292 --> 00:55:17.726
We're moving.

416
00:55:17.795 --> 00:55:21.595
- What?
- The ship is moving. I can feel it.

417
00:55:22.099 --> 00:55:26.160
The ship has stealth-run.
There's no way you can tell.

418
00:55:27.071 --> 00:55:30.632
- She's right.
- The ship's been go since the attack.

419
00:55:30.741 --> 00:55:33.437
It's a standard emergency procedure.

420
00:55:33.511 --> 00:55:37.675
That's right. Any serious problem.
the ship autopilots to home base.

421
00:55:37.782 --> 00:55:40.444
And you were planning on
letting us know this?

422
00:55:40.518 --> 00:55:42.782
Nobody asked.

423
00:55:42.853 --> 00:55:45.287
What's home base?

424
00:55:47.858 --> 00:55:50.190
Earth.

425
00:55:50.294 --> 00:55:52.489
- Great!
- Bastard!

426
00:55:52.596 --> 00:55:56.123
Earth? I'd rather stay here
with the things. man.

427
00:55:56.867 --> 00:56:00.166
- How long until we get to Earth?
- Three hours almost.

428
00:56:00.271 --> 00:56:02.364
We gotta blow the ship.

429
00:56:02.473 --> 00:56:05.271
Call! You're not blowing this ship.

430
00:56:06.010 --> 00:56:08.604
Not while we're on it. OK?

431
00:56:08.679 --> 00:56:13.207
You get out of the ship
you do as you please. all right?

432
00:56:13.784 --> 00:56:16.878
Earth. man. What a shithole.

433
00:56:24.829 --> 00:56:26.888
It's clear.

434
00:56:32.903 --> 00:56:34.996
Hey. Ripley.

435
00:56:38.676 --> 00:56:43.306
I heard you. like.
ran into these things before.

436
00:56:43.380 --> 00:56:46.747
- That's right.
- Wow. man.

437
00:56:46.851 --> 00:56:49.342
So. like. what did you do?

438
00:56:53.023 --> 00:56:55.082
I died.

439
00:57:21.385 --> 00:57:23.546
Not that way!

440
00:57:29.059 --> 00:57:31.118
Ripley.

441
00:57:37.368 --> 00:57:39.427
Ripley. come on.

442
00:57:41.772 --> 00:57:44.798
Ripley. we got no time for sightseeing here.

443
00:57:49.380 --> 00:57:51.746
Ripley. don't.

444
00:59:53.170 --> 00:59:55.229
Kill...

445
00:59:55.839 --> 00:59:56.863
me.

446
01:00:07.051 --> 01:00:09.349
Kill me.

447
01:01:51.121 --> 01:01:53.385
Don't do it. Ripley.

448
01:02:00.731 --> 01:02:02.824
Don't do what?

449
01:02:14.878 --> 01:02:17.574
What's the big deal. man?

450
01:02:17.681 --> 01:02:19.740
Fuckin' waste of ammo.

451
01:02:19.850 --> 01:02:21.909
Let's go.

452
01:02:23.587 --> 01:02:25.748
Must be a chick thing.

453
01:03:35.592 --> 01:03:38.959
Am I dreaming. or is this not
the shit we brought with us?

454
01:03:39.062 --> 01:03:41.656
Yeah. It's the same shit.

455
01:03:42.599 --> 01:03:46.228
It stinks in here. man. Let's keep moving.

456
01:04:15.999 --> 01:04:18.297
Get away from me!

457
01:04:18.368 --> 01:04:19.835
Get away!

458
01:04:19.937 --> 01:04:21.837
Get away from me!

459
01:04:21.939 --> 01:04:23.804
- Drop the rod.
- Get away from me!

460
01:04:23.874 --> 01:04:27.207
- Do it!
- Get away from me.

461
01:04:29.279 --> 01:04:32.214
Get away from me.

462
01:04:32.316 --> 01:04:34.546
Who are you people?

463
01:04:35.118 --> 01:04:37.712
- What's happening here?
- Calm down.

464
01:04:37.821 --> 01:04:42.622
What's happening here is that
we're getting the fuck off this ghost ship. OK?

465
01:04:42.693 --> 01:04:44.786
Ship? What ship?

466
01:04:46.063 --> 01:04:48.156
Where am I?

467
01:04:48.232 --> 01:04:51.998
I was in cryo. right?
On my way to Xarem. right?

468
01:04:52.069 --> 01:04:54.663
Work crew for the nickel refinery. right?

469
01:04:54.738 --> 01:04:58.071
I wake up...
I know I don't understand.

470
01:04:59.676 --> 01:05:01.701
Oh. God. I...

471
01:05:01.812 --> 01:05:04.747
I saw... I saw horrible things.

472
01:05:05.482 --> 01:05:09.680
Look. you're coming with us.
It's too dangerous for you here.

473
01:05:19.997 --> 01:05:21.658
Leave him.

474
01:05:21.732 --> 01:05:24.758
Fuck you! We're not leaving him here.

475
01:05:24.868 --> 01:05:28.770
He's got one inside of him. I can smell it.

476
01:05:31.742 --> 01:05:33.539
Inside me?

477
01:05:35.245 --> 01:05:37.839
Inside me? What's inside me?

478
01:05:37.914 --> 01:05:41.281
I don't want one of those things
birthing anywhere near my ass.

479
01:05:41.385 --> 01:05:45.344
- It's a bad risk.
- What's inside me?

480
01:05:45.422 --> 01:05:49.290
- We can'tjust leave him here.
- You came here to stop 'em spreading.

481
01:05:49.393 --> 01:05:51.987
- What's inside me?
- Can't you stop it?

482
01:05:52.062 --> 01:05:54.758
- We've got no time.
- We can't do it here.

483
01:05:56.753 --> 01:05:58.516
I could do him. Back of the head.

484
01:06:00.777 --> 01:06:03.473
- What's inside me?
- There's got to be another way.

485
01:06:03.580 --> 01:06:06.777
- What if we freeze him?
- What's in-fucking-side me?

486
01:06:06.884 --> 01:06:09.114
A parasite!

487
01:06:11.154 --> 01:06:13.554
A foreign element.

488
01:06:18.095 --> 01:06:21.258
There's a monster in your chest.

489
01:06:21.331 --> 01:06:24.494
These guys hijacked your ship.

490
01:06:24.601 --> 01:06:29.504
and they sold your cryotube to this human.

491
01:06:29.606 --> 01:06:32.166
And he put an alien inside of you.

492
01:06:32.843 --> 01:06:34.936
It's a really nasty one.

493
01:06:35.812 --> 01:06:40.112
And in a few hours. it will burst its way
through your ribcage.

494
01:06:40.918 --> 01:06:42.783
and you're gonna die.

495
01:06:48.492 --> 01:06:50.983
Any questions?

496
01:06:57.134 --> 01:06:59.102
Who are you?

497
01:07:00.704 --> 01:07:03.798
I'm the monster's mother.

498
01:07:06.810 --> 01:07:10.268
If we freeze him on the Betty.
the doctor can remove it later.

499
01:07:10.347 --> 01:07:13.805
- Fine by me.
- Since when were you in goddamn charge?

500
01:07:13.884 --> 01:07:15.977
Since you were born without balls!

501
01:07:16.053 --> 01:07:18.317
Ease off. people!

502
01:07:26.330 --> 01:07:30.323
All right. you come with us.
You might even live.

503
01:07:30.734 --> 01:07:33.532
Get twitchy on me. you'll be shot.

504
01:07:34.338 --> 01:07:36.397
Let's move out.

505
01:07:47.217 --> 01:07:49.879
It's a mess down there. Is this the only way?

506
01:07:49.987 --> 01:07:52.979
Vriess! We gotta lose the chair.

507
01:07:55.692 --> 01:07:57.751
I know.

508
01:07:57.861 --> 01:08:02.093
- Kawlang maneuver. right?
- Yeah. Just like old times.

509
01:08:02.199 --> 01:08:04.258
Yeah.

510
01:08:08.071 --> 01:08:10.403
Must be the cooling tanks.

511
01:08:10.507 --> 01:08:12.998
Somebody must have opened the valves.

512
01:08:13.110 --> 01:08:16.045
The nasties couldn't do that. could they?

513
01:08:27.724 --> 01:08:30.352
We're at the bottom of the ship.

514
01:08:30.427 --> 01:08:33.692
We have to go through the kitchen.
Maybe 90ft.

515
01:08:33.764 --> 01:08:36.289
To the elevator on the other side.

516
01:08:37.768 --> 01:08:40.601
- I don't like it.
- What's to like?

517
01:08:42.239 --> 01:08:46.369
- This sucks!
- Wren. are you sure about the distance?

518
01:08:46.443 --> 01:08:47.774
Yes!

519
01:08:48.945 --> 01:08:52.278
- You ready to get wet. partner?
- Yeah.

520
01:09:00.424 --> 01:09:04.121
Hey. will your weapons fly underwater?

521
01:09:04.227 --> 01:09:06.718
They're disposables. They can take it.

522
01:09:06.797 --> 01:09:08.264
Disposables?

523
01:09:12.669 --> 01:09:15.103
Hey. I heard about those.

524
01:09:17.074 --> 01:09:20.066
- How many rounds?
- 20.

525
01:09:20.143 --> 01:09:24.773
Split points give you a good hole.
even if it's smaller caliber.

526
01:09:24.848 --> 01:09:26.076
That's cool!

527
01:09:27.918 --> 01:09:31.115
They're big with hitters
'cause you throw 'em away after the job.

528
01:09:31.188 --> 01:09:34.248
I wouldn't like to throw away a weapon
I'm attached to.

529
01:09:34.324 --> 01:09:36.019
Yeah.

530
01:09:36.126 --> 01:09:39.926
Guess I don't have to tell everyone
to take a deep breath.

531
01:09:46.688 --> 01:09:52.251
When we hit the surface. no backstroke. OK?

532
01:13:25.474 --> 01:13:27.339
Jesus Christ!

533
01:13:39.688 --> 01:13:43.488
They set a goddamn trap.
It's a goddamn ambush!

534
01:14:49.691 --> 01:14:51.352
Distephano!

535
01:15:11.613 --> 01:15:14.878
It won't break.
Give me your weapon.

536
01:15:15.884 --> 01:15:18.512
You really are way too trusting.

537
01:15:18.587 --> 01:15:19.781
No!

538
01:15:29.764 --> 01:15:31.231
No!

539
01:15:39.774 --> 01:15:42.800
You killed her! You bastard!

540
01:15:47.716 --> 01:15:49.877
I'll get you!

541
01:15:51.653 --> 01:15:53.746
Father. lock the door!

542
01:16:09.271 --> 01:16:12.138
Christie! Climb!

543
01:16:12.240 --> 01:16:13.798
Climb! Come on!

544
01:16:14.175 --> 01:16:16.109
Come on!

545
01:16:16.177 --> 01:16:18.975
It's jammed! Move it!

546
01:16:19.080 --> 01:16:21.139
It's jammed!

547
01:16:53.848 --> 01:16:56.282
Get off my foot. bitch!

548
01:17:09.030 --> 01:17:10.895
Johner!

549
01:17:10.999 --> 01:17:13.160
Get off me!

550
01:17:14.703 --> 01:17:15.692
Johner!

551
01:17:20.475 --> 01:17:22.534
Die. motherfucker!

552
01:17:24.579 --> 01:17:26.376
Do it. man!

553
01:17:43.498 --> 01:17:45.932
Real nice party. ain't it?

554
01:18:14.562 --> 01:18:15.756
Christie!

555
01:18:16.564 --> 01:18:18.088
Christie!

556
01:18:19.134 --> 01:18:20.396
Christie!

557
01:18:20.468 --> 01:18:22.026
No!

558
01:18:22.103 --> 01:18:23.798
Christie!

559
01:18:24.539 --> 01:18:26.473
Christie!

560
01:18:26.574 --> 01:18:30.066
What are you doing? Don't do it!

561
01:18:30.145 --> 01:18:31.442
Don't!

562
01:18:31.546 --> 01:18:33.605
We can make it!

563
01:18:34.549 --> 01:18:36.141
No!

564
01:18:40.488 --> 01:18:42.581
Damn!

565
01:19:29.504 --> 01:19:31.597
This way.

566
01:19:33.808 --> 01:19:35.036
Come on!

567
01:19:41.116 --> 01:19:43.175
Baby. am I glad to see you!

568
01:19:43.284 --> 01:19:46.048
I was sure that asshole got you. Are you hurt?

569
01:19:46.154 --> 01:19:48.213
I'm fine.

570
01:19:48.323 --> 01:19:51.690
- You got body armour on?
- Yeah. Come on.

571
01:19:51.793 --> 01:19:54.626
You took it in the chest. I saw it.

572
01:20:16.384 --> 01:20:18.477
You're a robot?

573
01:20:19.554 --> 01:20:23.081
Son of a bitch! Our little Call
is just full of surprises.

574
01:20:23.191 --> 01:20:27.252
I should've known.
No human being is that humane.

575
01:20:27.362 --> 01:20:29.887
I thought synthetics were logical.

576
01:20:29.998 --> 01:20:32.432
You just a big old psycho. girl!

577
01:20:32.534 --> 01:20:36.095
- You're a robot?
- You're a Second Gen. aren't you?

578
01:20:37.338 --> 01:20:39.499
You're an Auton.

579
01:20:39.574 --> 01:20:42.702
Robots designed by robots. right?

580
01:20:42.777 --> 01:20:45.871
- Ha!
- That's right. I remember.

581
01:20:45.947 --> 01:20:48.939
They were meant to revitalise
the synthetic industry.

582
01:20:49.050 --> 01:20:51.177
Instead they buried it.

583
01:20:51.953 --> 01:20:54.513
They don't like being told what to do.

584
01:20:54.589 --> 01:20:56.784
The government ordered a recall.

585
01:20:56.891 --> 01:20:58.950
Now. I heard...

586
01:20:59.060 --> 01:21:02.427
I heard that only a few
had gotten out in time.

587
01:21:02.564 --> 01:21:05.761
Man. I never thought that I would see one!

588
01:21:05.867 --> 01:21:09.268
Great. She's a toaster oven.

589
01:21:09.971 --> 01:21:12.064
Can we leave now?

590
01:21:13.942 --> 01:21:17.275
- How long before we land?
- Two hours.

591
01:21:17.378 --> 01:21:20.905
Vriess. you got a wrench?
Maybe she just needs an oil change.

592
01:21:20.982 --> 01:21:23.041
Sorry. Access denied.

593
01:21:23.117 --> 01:21:27.110
- And I almost fucked it.
- Like you never fucked a robot!

594
01:21:27.222 --> 01:21:30.055
If Wren gets in the computer.
he could screw us.

595
01:21:30.124 --> 01:21:33.457
- We gotta find a terminal.
- There's no console on this level.

596
01:21:33.561 --> 01:21:36.394
- We'd have to go back.
- We can't go back.

597
01:21:36.464 --> 01:21:39.729
- And I don't know Wren's access codes.
- Help me.

598
01:21:41.402 --> 01:21:42.994
Call...

599
01:21:44.005 --> 01:21:46.098
No. I can't.

600
01:21:46.174 --> 01:21:50.440
Right. You're the new model droid.
You can access the mainframe by remote.

601
01:21:50.511 --> 01:21:54.277
No. I can't.
I burned my modem. We all did.

602
01:21:54.349 --> 01:21:58.251
Call. you can still patch in manually.
You know that.

603
01:21:58.987 --> 01:22:02.320
There's ports in the chapel. up there.

604
01:22:03.524 --> 01:22:05.185
Call...

605
01:22:10.498 --> 01:22:14.195
- You're programmed for that?
- Don't make me do this.

606
01:22:14.302 --> 01:22:17.430
Don't make me make you.

607
01:22:17.505 --> 01:22:19.973
I don't wanna go in there.

608
01:22:20.041 --> 01:22:22.839
It's like my insides are liquid. It's not real.

609
01:22:22.944 --> 01:22:27.278
Get over it. You can blow this ship.
before it reaches Earth.

610
01:22:27.949 --> 01:22:30.281
and kill them all.

611
01:22:39.661 --> 01:22:42.357
Just give us time to get out first.

612
01:22:45.533 --> 01:22:47.524
- Damn it!
- Anything?

613
01:22:47.635 --> 01:22:49.364
Hold on.

614
01:22:53.708 --> 01:22:57.667
Breach in sector seven. sector three.

615
01:22:57.745 --> 01:22:59.838
Sector nine unstable.

616
01:23:01.249 --> 01:23:03.740
Engines operating at 41%.

617
01:23:03.851 --> 01:23:07.082
86 minutes until Earth dock.

618
01:23:07.188 --> 01:23:09.349
We burned too much energy.

619
01:23:09.424 --> 01:23:13.417
I can't make critical mass. I can't blow it.

620
01:23:13.528 --> 01:23:15.155
Then crash it.

621
01:23:28.843 --> 01:23:31.175
I'm OK. I'm OK.

622
01:23:35.523 --> 01:23:36.990
I feel good.

623
01:23:38.996 --> 01:23:41.294
Ground level recalibrated.

624
01:23:41.365 --> 01:23:46.359
New destination: 7-6-0-4-0-3.
Uninhabited quadrant.

625
01:23:47.004 --> 01:23:51.600
Braking system's offline.
Deceleration increase.

626
01:23:52.510 --> 01:23:56.276
Time until impact
now 43 minutes. 8 seconds.

627
01:23:58.282 --> 01:24:00.512
Try to clear us a path to the Betty.

628
01:24:01.485 --> 01:24:03.350
And start her up.

629
01:24:33.441 --> 01:24:36.410
Please wait.

630
01:24:40.048 --> 01:24:43.449
Emergency override
in console 45V. level one.

631
01:24:47.122 --> 01:24:49.352
It's Wren. He's almost at the Betty.

632
01:25:02.804 --> 01:25:06.365
Father. locate the power drain. Report.

633
01:25:08.777 --> 01:25:10.870
Father?

634
01:25:11.313 --> 01:25:13.406
Father?

635
01:25:17.385 --> 01:25:20.149
Father's dead. asshole.

636
01:25:23.625 --> 01:25:29.393
Intruder on level one.
All aliens. please proceed to level one.

637
01:25:29.464 --> 01:25:31.557
You got a mean streak.

638
01:25:35.937 --> 01:25:37.905
Damn it!

639
01:25:37.973 --> 01:25:40.237
- Let me see.
- Don't touch me.

640
01:25:40.308 --> 01:25:42.640
Come on.

641
01:25:42.744 --> 01:25:45.338
You must think this is pretty funny.

642
01:25:46.581 --> 01:25:49.573
I'm finding a lot of things funny lately.

643
01:25:49.651 --> 01:25:51.744
But I don't think they are.

644
01:25:59.694 --> 01:26:01.787
Why do you go on living?

645
01:26:04.266 --> 01:26:06.791
How can you stand being what you are?

646
01:26:08.637 --> 01:26:11.197
Not much choice.

647
01:26:14.309 --> 01:26:16.869
At least there's a part of you that's human.

648
01:26:18.146 --> 01:26:19.773
I'm just...

649
01:26:19.848 --> 01:26:21.213
Look at me.

650
01:26:22.150 --> 01:26:24.380
I'm disgusting.

651
01:26:26.054 --> 01:26:28.522
Why did you come here?

652
01:26:28.623 --> 01:26:30.853
To kill you. Remember?

653
01:26:30.959 --> 01:26:33.018
Before the recall.

654
01:26:33.128 --> 01:26:36.188
I accessed the mainframe.

655
01:26:36.298 --> 01:26:40.462
Every dirty little covert op
the government ever dreamed up is in there.

656
01:26:40.535 --> 01:26:45.165
And this. you. the aliens.
even the crew from the Betty.

657
01:26:45.240 --> 01:26:48.368
I knew if they succeeded
it'd be the end of them.

658
01:26:50.817 --> 01:26:52.808
- Why do you care?
- I'm programmed to.

659
01:26:54.809 --> 01:26:56.834
You're programmed to be an asshole?

660
01:26:58.012 --> 01:27:01.106
You're the new asshole model
they're putting out?

661
01:27:01.182 --> 01:27:02.649
Come on.

662
01:27:04.652 --> 01:27:07.212
I couldn't watch 'em do it.

663
01:27:07.321 --> 01:27:10.984
I couldn't let 'em annihilate themselves.

664
01:27:11.058 --> 01:27:13.151
Do you understand that?

665
01:27:16.463 --> 01:27:18.294
I did once.

666
01:27:18.365 --> 01:27:21.198
I tried to save people.

667
01:27:22.169 --> 01:27:24.729
It didn't work out.

668
01:27:24.839 --> 01:27:27.399
There was this girl.

669
01:27:30.010 --> 01:27:32.877
She had bad dreams.

670
01:27:32.980 --> 01:27:35.847
I tried to help her.

671
01:27:35.916 --> 01:27:38.009
She died.

672
01:27:39.086 --> 01:27:42.021
Now I can't even remember her name.

673
01:27:46.727 --> 01:27:48.820
I guess we're almost there.

674
01:27:48.896 --> 01:27:50.989
Right.

675
01:27:52.566 --> 01:27:57.663
- Do you dream?
- I... We have neural processors. Yes.

676
01:27:58.572 --> 01:28:02.167
When I sleep I dream about them. It.

677
01:28:02.243 --> 01:28:03.938
Every night.

678
01:28:04.044 --> 01:28:06.410
All around me. In me.

679
01:28:06.513 --> 01:28:09.880
I used to be afraid to dream.
but I'm not anymore.

680
01:28:09.950 --> 01:28:12.418
Why?

681
01:28:12.519 --> 01:28:19.425
Because. no matter how bad the dreams get.
when I wake up it's always worse.

682
01:28:22.029 --> 01:28:25.123
- It's not so far now!
- God. I'm so tired!

683
01:28:38.045 --> 01:28:40.479
Oh. no. This is bad. right?

684
01:28:41.115 --> 01:28:43.276
I think we're near the nest.

685
01:28:43.350 --> 01:28:46.183
- We'll go another way.
- We don't have time.

686
01:28:46.287 --> 01:28:48.346
- We got 90 minutes.
- Not any more.

687
01:28:48.455 --> 01:28:50.286
What?

688
01:28:50.357 --> 01:28:53.383
- What did you do. robot?
- Let's go. Come on.

689
01:28:53.494 --> 01:28:57.897
Hey! You wanna die here with
your brothers and sisters. that's cool.

690
01:28:57.998 --> 01:29:00.296
But I plan to live past today.

691
01:29:00.367 --> 01:29:02.995
If this hunk of plastic is pullin' any shit.

692
01:29:03.070 --> 01:29:05.163
I'm gonna kill her!

693
01:29:06.140 --> 01:29:07.801
Kill you!

694
01:29:07.875 --> 01:29:11.504
Does that compute?
Or do I have to draw you a schematic?

695
01:29:12.246 --> 01:29:13.679
Hey!

696
01:29:16.483 --> 01:29:18.713
You want another souvenir?

697
01:29:26.026 --> 01:29:28.824
- How far are the docks?
- 100 yards.

698
01:29:40.040 --> 01:29:42.099
Ripley?

699
01:29:43.110 --> 01:29:45.203
Ripley?

700
01:29:46.080 --> 01:29:48.207
Come on!

701
01:29:48.282 --> 01:29:50.375
Ripley. we have to go.

702
01:29:52.186 --> 01:29:56.088
I hear them. I hear them. They're so close.

703
01:29:57.091 --> 01:29:59.252
- Ripley...
- It's the queen.

704
01:30:00.027 --> 01:30:02.461
She's in pain.

705
01:30:05.466 --> 01:30:07.559
Ripley!

706
01:30:07.901 --> 01:30:10.062
Ripley!

707
01:30:10.137 --> 01:30:12.230
Wait!

708
01:30:34.228 --> 01:30:35.627
Oh. my God.

709
01:30:48.742 --> 01:30:53.839
We gotta be moving. The best thing
we can do is pray for a quick death.

710
01:30:53.947 --> 01:30:56.848
Come on. Come on.

711
01:30:56.950 --> 01:31:01.444
- It's not right.
- I've been saying that all day.

712
01:31:58.539 --> 01:32:04.876
Call. I need you to patch into
the ship again. and open the hatch.

713
01:32:14.488 --> 01:32:17.651
Johner. we should put Purvis
in the freezer now.

714
01:32:17.725 --> 01:32:19.716
All right. little buddy.

715
01:32:20.761 --> 01:32:23.195
Nap time.

716
01:32:29.937 --> 01:32:34.374
Nobody moves. or I put a cap
right where this little droid's brain is.

717
01:32:35.276 --> 01:32:39.679
- Distephano. take the weapons.
- Begging your pardon. sir. but fuck you!

718
01:32:39.747 --> 01:32:42.113
Fine. Then I kill her.

719
01:32:42.216 --> 01:32:44.878
and you kill me. and we all die.

720
01:32:44.952 --> 01:32:46.579
and nobody goes home!

721
01:32:46.687 --> 01:32:48.746
Now drop the weapon!

722
01:32:53.627 --> 01:32:58.360
Then this little synthetic bitch
is gonna plug into the Auriga

723
01:32:58.432 --> 01:33:03.267
and she is gonna take us back to home base.
according to standard emergency procedures.

724
01:33:03.370 --> 01:33:06.032
- No. she's not!
- Are you crazy?

725
01:33:06.106 --> 01:33:08.734
You still wanna bring those things
back to Earth?

726
01:33:08.809 --> 01:33:12.472
- Haven't you been paying attention?
- The intellectual speaks!

727
01:33:13.647 --> 01:33:17.083
- Listen. if...
- Don't you ever shut up?

728
01:33:29.430 --> 01:33:32.593
Why does nobody listen to me?

729
01:34:15.609 --> 01:34:20.046
I told you. at first everything was normal.
The queen laid her eggs.

730
01:34:20.147 --> 01:34:25.449
But then she started to change.
She added a second cycle. so...

731
01:34:27.721 --> 01:34:29.814
So...

732
01:34:33.794 --> 01:34:36.194
this time there is no host.

733
01:34:37.231 --> 01:34:39.699
There are no eggs.

734
01:34:39.800 --> 01:34:43.497
There is only her womb

735
01:34:43.570 --> 01:34:46.368
and the creature inside.

736
01:34:46.473 --> 01:34:53.037
That is Ripley's gift to her:
a human reproductive system.

737
01:34:53.147 --> 01:34:56.480
She is giving birth for you. Ripley.

738
01:34:56.550 --> 01:34:59.747
And now she is perfect!

739
01:36:26.073 --> 01:36:28.234
You are...

740
01:36:29.810 --> 01:36:35.840
a beautiful butterfly.

741
01:37:03.844 --> 01:37:04.970
No!

742
01:37:09.883 --> 01:37:11.373
No! No...

743
01:38:05.939 --> 01:38:07.668
Look.

744
01:38:07.741 --> 01:38:12.576
Your beautiful. beautiful little baby.

745
01:38:13.614 --> 01:38:15.878
Look. it thinks you're its mother.

746
01:38:21.221 --> 01:38:22.415
Come on.

747
01:38:23.524 --> 01:38:25.583
Come on.

748
01:38:33.433 --> 01:38:34.593
Come on.

749
01:38:52.786 --> 01:38:56.517
Civilian vessel online.
Emergency departure authorised.

750
01:39:01.295 --> 01:39:05.823
All right. she's hot. I'll open the Auriga's
air locks. Pull the holding clamps.

751
01:39:05.933 --> 01:39:11.428
Right. I just need to find
the vertical thrust lock.

752
01:39:16.643 --> 01:39:19.510
- Are you sure you can fly this thing?
- Yes!

753
01:39:33.794 --> 01:39:36.490
Launch status is go.

754
01:39:36.597 --> 01:39:37.325
No!

755
01:39:39.099 --> 01:39:40.999
Ripley!

756
01:40:09.396 --> 01:40:11.387
- Hey.
- I thought you were dead.

757
01:40:11.498 --> 01:40:13.864
I get that a lot.

758
01:40:13.967 --> 01:40:20.338
- Why are we still here?
- I'm just finding the manual override.

759
01:40:20.407 --> 01:40:22.398
- For Christ's sake!
- Hey. Ripley.

760
01:40:22.509 --> 01:40:24.500
Good memory. Excuse me.

761
01:40:24.578 --> 01:40:26.307
- Ripley's back.
- Is that it?

762
01:40:26.380 --> 01:40:27.244
Nope.

763
01:40:28.515 --> 01:40:30.642
You can't fly one of these things?

764
01:40:30.717 --> 01:40:34.084
Are you kidding?
This piece of shit is older than I am.

765
01:40:34.187 --> 01:40:37.588
Goddammit! We still got breach. The hatch.

766
01:40:37.691 --> 01:40:40.717
- I closed it.
- I've fixed it a hundred times!

767
01:40:40.827 --> 01:40:43.557
I'll get it. I'll get it.

768
01:41:04.718 --> 01:41:11.954
Approaching Earth's atmosphere.
Window of departure now 46 seconds.

769
01:41:13.360 --> 01:41:16.261
Call? We have to go.

770
01:41:17.297 --> 01:41:19.356
Call.

771
01:41:21.468 --> 01:41:23.732
We've gotta get out of here.

772
01:41:28.408 --> 01:41:32.367
Window of departure now 20 seconds.

773
01:41:35.882 --> 01:41:39.374
Grab on to something. Call. We're outta here.

774
01:41:54.668 --> 01:41:55.828
Come on. baby.

775
01:42:09.616 --> 01:42:12.312
This thing is gonna fall apart!

776
01:42:12.419 --> 01:42:14.649
Pressure's unstable!

777
01:42:19.626 --> 01:42:22.857
Go help Call turn on the auxiliary pump!

778
01:42:50.290 --> 01:42:51.780
Distephano?

779
01:43:12.846 --> 01:43:14.541
Come on! Step on it!

780
01:43:15.182 --> 01:43:18.310
Hey! I'm not the mechanic here. Ironside!

781
01:43:18.385 --> 01:43:20.979
I mostly just hurt people!

782
01:43:21.054 --> 01:43:22.385
Shit!

783
01:43:22.489 --> 01:43:24.753
Call!

784
01:43:24.858 --> 01:43:27.156
Call. get back up here!

785
01:43:28.762 --> 01:43:31.424
Call! Call!

786
01:43:32.399 --> 01:43:33.388
Ripley!

787
01:43:33.500 --> 01:43:36.162
Hey. Ripley!

788
01:43:40.941 --> 01:43:45.105
Johner. where are you. you son of a bitch?
Get on it. bastard!

789
01:43:45.212 --> 01:43:47.976
- What am I supposed to do?
- Grab the sticks!

790
01:44:03.230 --> 01:44:05.596
Put her down.

791
01:45:42.462 --> 01:45:44.657
Ripley!

792
01:46:11.558 --> 01:46:13.492
I'm sorry.

793
01:46:43.556 --> 01:46:47.925
USM Auriga will impact in five seconds. Four.

794
01:46:48.862 --> 01:46:50.090
Three.

795
01:46:50.196 --> 01:46:51.458
Two.

796
01:46:51.564 --> 01:46:52.588
One.

797
01:46:52.699 --> 01:46:53.791
Thank you.

798
01:47:18.625 --> 01:47:20.820
- What's burning?
- Us!

799
01:47:23.296 --> 01:47:25.264
Shit! You're right!

800
01:48:46.068 --> 01:48:48.559
So this is Earth. huh?

801
01:48:50.506 --> 01:48:52.599
This is Earth.

802
01:48:55.945 --> 01:48:58.004
It's my first time here.

803
01:49:02.418 --> 01:49:06.912
I suppose the military'll be
sniffing around here pretty soon.

804
01:49:06.989 --> 01:49:09.685
Bet you're not too anxious to see them.

805
01:49:09.792 --> 01:49:11.851
Not really.

806
01:49:12.862 --> 01:49:18.164
You know. a person could get pretty lost
around here if they wanted to.

807
01:49:18.968 --> 01:49:21.129
What do you think?

808
01:49:21.203 --> 01:49:24.036
What shall we do?

809
01:49:24.139 --> 01:49:26.198
I don't know.

810
01:49:27.543 --> 01:49:29.909
I'm a stranger here myself.

811
01:55:59.534 --> 01:56:03.300
Visiontext Subtitles: Stephanie Donohue

812
01:56:03.372 --> 01:56:05.465
US ENGLISH
